# The global ignore at ~/.config/git/ignore excludes .claude/ wholesale, which
# is sensible for ordinary projects but wrong here: this repository exists to
# keep Claude Code configuration under version control, and CLAUDE.md requires
# that none of its documentation be ignored by git configuration. A repository
# .gitignore takes precedence over core.excludesFile, so this negation wins.
!.claude/

# Transient worktrees. Each is a full checkout of this repository, so committing
# one would nest the repo inside itself. Listed after the negation above because
# git applies the last matching pattern.
.claude/worktrees/
